# Files Vercel must never upload or bundle into a function.
#
# Git-based deploys already skip everything in .gitignore, so this matters for
# two cases: `vercel dev` / `vercel deploy` from a laptop, which upload the
# working directory as it actually is, and anything that slipped past
# .gitignore.
#
# The Python bundle limit is 500 MB uncompressed. A clean install of
# backend/requirements.txt is ~95 MB, but a developer's backend/.venv
# accumulates far more than that over a project's life - measured at 263 MB on
# one machine, most of it packages no longer in requirements.txt. There is no
# tree-shaking for Python, so anything reachable at build time gets bundled.

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
backend/.venv/
backend/venv/
backend/tests/
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/.coverage
backend/htmlcov/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Development-only: drops and recreates every table. Must not be reachable
# from a deployed function.
backend/dev_reset_db.py

# --- Node -----------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/coverage/

# --- Tests and tooling not needed to build or run -------------------------
e2e/
.github/

# --- Local development only -----------------------------------------------
docker-compose.yml
start.bat
stop.bat
.claude/

# --- Docs -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.md
!latex/*.md
product.md
prompt.txt
resume-template.tex
